Build the IPQ9574 PCS into the kernel. As a module it loads at about 12 s
together with the PPE, and the QCA8084 clock controller (which now waits
for pcs0) then comes too late: the PHYs are attached with the generic
driver before the QCA8084 driver can bind. Built in, pcs0 probes at boot
and the whole chain (PCS, clock controller, PHY driver) is done long
before the PPE module loads. kmod-pcs-qcom-ipq9574 becomes an empty
package (OpenWrt notices the module is built-in).
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/config-default
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/config-default
@@ -56,3 +56,4 @@
 CONFIG_SPMI_MSM_PMIC_ARB=y
 # CONFIG_SPMI_PMIC_CLKDIV is not set
 CONFIG_MTD_OOPS=y
+CONFIG_PCS_QCOM_IPQ9574=y
